        "description": "<p>Galerio is a photo and video gallery plugin for elementor addons. There are multiple types of layouts and designs.</p>\n<p>Live Demo: <a href=\"https://star-addons.mhrtheme.com/galerio\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Check here</a></p>\n<p>Buy Pro Version: <a href=\"#\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Check here</a></p>\n",
        "installation": "<h4>From the dashboard:</h4>\n<ol>\n<li>Go to the WordPress Dashboard &#8220;Add New Plugin&#8221; section</li>\n<li>Search For &#8220;Galerio&#8221;</li>\n<li>Install, then Activate it</li>\n</ol>\n<h4>From the control panel:</h4>\n<ol>\n<li>Unzip (if it is zipped) and Upload <code>galerio</code> folder to the <code>/wp-content/plugins/</code> directory</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin through the &#8216;Plugins&#8217; menu in WordPress</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id='can%20i%20use%20the%20plugin%20without%20elementor%20website%20builder%3F'>\nCan I use the plugin without Elementor Website Builder?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>No. You cannot use without Elementor since it&#8217;s an addon for Elementor.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id='does%20it%20work%20with%20any%20theme%3F'>\nDoes it work with any theme?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Absolutely! It will work with any theme where Elementor works.</p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>1.0.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial stable realese</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
